# The Wandering Emperor: "-2: Exile target tapped creature. You gain 2 life." Bot2's Llanowar Elves attack on turn 4 and are
# tapped by attacking. Bot1 flashes the Emperor in during that declare-attackers step (a Black Lotus and a Plains pay), the turn
# she entered so she may activate at instant speed, and uses -2 on the tapped Elves: they are exiled, Bot1 is at 22 life and the
# Emperor at 1 loyalty. Bot2's Forest is untapped and is not an eligible target in any case.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
The Wandering Emperor
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
